    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 all tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added an optional `email` field to owners: syntactically validated, stored and returned lower-cased, with a 400 rejection when present but invalid.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added an optional `email` property (`format: email`, `maxLength: 255`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. This regenerates `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` (with `@Email`, `@Size`) and the MapStruct mapper maps `email` in both directions automatically.\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added the `email` column (`@Column(name = \"email\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 added the `email` column to the owners table in all four dialects (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres). Because hsqldb/mysql seed data used positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)`, I gave those inserts explicit column lists so they still load with the new column (h2/postgres already listed columns).\n\n4. **`OwnerEmails`** (new utility) \u2014 `normalize(String)`: leaves null/blank untouched (email is optional), else validates syntax via `^[^@\\s]+@[^@\\s]+\\.[^@\\s]+$` and returns the address lower-cased, throwing the checked `InvalidEmailException` when invalid.\n\n5. **`InvalidEmailException`** + **`InvalidEmailExceptionHandler`** + escalation YAML \u2014 modeled on the existing telephone pattern; responds 400 with `errors: [\"email\"]`.\n\n6. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `BuildOwner` (POST/create) and `ValidateOwner` (PUT/update, validates before load) both normalize the email; `ApplyOwner` copies the normalized email onto the entity on update.\n\nThe three new acceptance tests (`coreLowercasesEmail`, `errorRejectsInvalidEmail`, `functionalityAcceptsMissingEmail`) and the full suite are green.",
